asteroids A810: tell userland how many recoveries have happened

UNTESTED, not compiled. A recovery makes voided fences read as passed and the wait succeed (2015), so Chlorophyll publishes staging
whose copy never ran (recheck-audit finding 2). INFO.flags gains capability bit 0x20 and a recovery count in bits 16-31. The struct and
ABI minor stay the same, so no libdrm rebuild; old clients mask flags with 3. Client side: chlorophyll-epoch.patch in this folder.

Apply: git apply in the kernel tree (-p1). Independent of 2052; they touch different hunks.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
@@ -1552,7 +1552,8 @@
 		uint64_t v = 0;
 		sweet_gpu_lock();
 		r.info.abi_version = SWEET_GPU_ABI_VERSION;
-		r.info.flags = (sweet_gpu_ready() ? 1u : 2u) | (gSboAlias ? SWEET_GPU_INFO_CAP_SBO_ALIAS : 0u);
+		r.info.flags = (sweet_gpu_ready() ? 1u : 2u) | (gSboAlias ? SWEET_GPU_INFO_CAP_SBO_ALIAS : 0u) |
+		    SWEET_GPU_INFO_CAP_EPOCH | (sweet_gpu_epoch() << 16);
 		r.info.gpu_id = sweet_gpu_param(SWEET_MSM_PARAM_CHIP_ID, &v) && v != 0x06030001 ? 0 : 630;
 		r.info.chip_id = sweet_gpu_param(SWEET_MSM_PARAM_CHIP_ID, &v) ? (uint32_t)v : 0x06030001;
 		r.info.va_start = sweet_gpu_param(SWEET_MSM_PARAM_VA_START, &v) ? v : 0;
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdrenoABI.h
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdrenoABI.h
@@ -173,6 +173,9 @@
 /* INFO.flags capability bits (bit0/bit1 above are ready/lost; capabilities start at bit 4). */
 #define SWEET_GPU_INFO_CAP_SBO_ALIAS    0x10    /* minor 2: SBO_IN_WRITABLE_ALIAS works (absent when boot-arg sweetgpualias=0) */
 
+/* 2053: INFO.flags bits 16-31 count GPU recoveries. A recovery makes voided fences read as passed, so a waiter cannot see it. */
+#define SWEET_GPU_INFO_CAP_EPOCH        0x20
+
 /* IOSurface memory as a BO: the pages of the surface (pixels from byte 0 of its memory) are entered into the
  * GPU address space. On input handle = SWEET_GPU_DESCRIBE_ONLY asks only for the geometry (no BO is made). */
 #define SWEET_GPU_DESCRIBE_ONLY         0xffffffffu
